# <%= name %>

A Roblox game built with [KRF](https://kevmp.github.io/KRF/) `<%= runtime.package %>@<%= runtime.version %>`.

## Setup

```bash
npm install
npm run build
```

`npm install` installs [Rokit](https://github.com/rojo-rbx/rokit) if you don't have it, the Roblox
tools pinned in `rokit.toml`, and the Wally packages. Wally records the resolved versions in
`wally.lock`; commit it. Open `<%= name %>.rbxl` in Roblox Studio and press Play.
Hold F (or X on a gamepad) to Focus: Energy regenerates while you hold it.
<% if (options.mode === "hybrid") { -%>

This is a Hybrid project: Rojo owns `src` and `Packages`, and your Studio place owns the world.
Save the built place somewhere else, keep building the world there, and sync code with `rojo serve`.
<% } -%>

## Scripts

| Script | Does |
| --- | --- |
| `npm run build` | Builds `<%= name %>.rbxl` |
| `npm run format` | Formats `src` |
| `npm run check` | Formats `src`, then lints and strict type checks |
| `npm run createAction` | Creates an Action in `src/server/Actions` |
| `npm run createTag` | Creates a Tag in `src/server/Tags` |
| `npm run createResource` | Creates a Resource in `src/server/Resources` |
| `npm run createController` | Creates a Controller in `src/server/Controllers` |
| `npm run createCommand` | Creates a Command in `src/server/Commands` |
| `npm run createHint` | Creates a Hint in `src/server/Hints` |
| `npm run createDomain` | Creates a replication domain in `src/server/ReplicationDomains` |

## Adding definitions

Each folder under `src/server` that `Startup.server.luau` passes to `KRF.Server.Init` has an
`init.luau` that loads every module beneath it, so a new module there loads on the next build.
The generators write a typed module for you:

```bash
npm run createAction -- --name Fireball --recipe channel --duration 2 --cost Energy=10 --yes
```

Every field a definition supports has a flag, such as `--required-tag`, `--requirement`,
`--lock`, `--hook`, `--property`, `--regen`, `--request-field` or `--event`; add `-- --help` to see
them all. Pass flags after `--`. Without `--yes`, the generator asks for everything you left out,
one question at a time, offering the Tags, Resources and Actions the project already has.
`--dry-run` shows the plan without writing, and `--json` prints one
result object (use `npm run --silent` to keep npm's banner out of it). The first Controller,
Command, Hint or replication domain also creates its folder's loader and adds it to
`Startup.server.luau`.

Players can request only the Actions declared in `src/shared/ActionRequests`. Like the definition
folders, its `init.luau` merges every module beneath it, one module per Action. `--requestable`
writes that module, and a `--recipe held` Action also gets a `WhileDown` policy module in
`src/client/ActionInputPolicies`. Then put the Action in an ability slot (see Controls below).

The generator never overwrites a file. If you have changed `Startup.server.luau` or a folder's
`init.luau` so that it cannot wire the new module safely, it still writes the module, leaves your
code unchanged, prints the lines to add, and exits with code 5. See
[Definition Generators](https://kevmp.github.io/KRF/definition-generators) for every option.

## Controls

Keys bind to ability slots, not to Actions. `src/client/Controls/Keybinds.luau` binds F and
ButtonX to `AbilitySlot1`; `src/client/Controls/Loadout.luau` decides which Action each slot
triggers. Call `Loadout.Equip("AbilitySlot1", actionId)` to swap the Action in a slot: the next
press uses it, without rebinding keys. `src/client/LocalCharacter.luau` finds the local
character's ActorView, which Controls selects as the Actor your input drives.
